1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,167
Every export shipment lives in ten places: a spreadsheet, the ERP, a shared drive and a dozen inboxes.

2
00:00:07,167 --> 00:00:12,111
EOT-PCS puts it in one controlled record, from proforma invoice to payment.

3
00:00:12,111 --> 00:00:17,056
Customer, order and invoice values come from Oracle, read-only. Nothing is re-keyed.

4
00:00:17,056 --> 00:00:22,000
Rules decide which documents each shipment needs: customer, country, Incoterms and transport.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,944
If a mandatory document is missing, the package simply can't be submitted.

6
00:00:26,944 --> 00:00:32,630
The person who prepared it can never approve it. AI findings are flagged first.

7
00:00:32,630 --> 00:00:37,574
Every upload is checksummed and versioned, and replacing one needs a reason.

8
00:00:37,574 --> 00:00:43,259
Balances, reminders and escalations run themselves, and every action is in the audit log.

9
00:00:43,259 --> 00:00:49,344
EOT-PCS is in pilot with BigMo. Book a walkthrough on your own document rules.
